    {
      "id": "a1-u03-d05-t01",
      "before": "a1-u03-d05-e01",
      "title": { "en": "Masculine and feminine" },
      "body": { "en": "Every Polish noun has a gender. A noun that ends in a consonant is usually masculine: *brat*, *problem*, *numer*. A noun that ends in *-a* is usually feminine: *mama*, *siostra*. A word for a man is masculine whatever its ending: *tata*." }
    },
    {
      "id": "a1-u03-d05-t02",
      "before": "a1-u03-d05-e08",
      "title": { "en": "Mój and moja" },
      "body": { "en": "\"My\" follows the gender of the noun, not of the person speaking. *Mój* goes with a masculine noun: *mój brat*, *mój tata*. *Moja* goes with a feminine noun: *moja mama*, *moja siostra*." }
    }
  ],
